{:edb/db-before-t 2477 :edb/db-after-t 2478 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535790 50 #inst "2026-10-09T07:18:42.063Z" 13194139535790 true] [17592186129054 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366406 13194139535790 true] [17592186366406 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366407 13194139535790 true] [17592186366406 1089 "q-38063" 13194139535790 true] [17592186366406 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535790 true] [17592186366406 1100 "The velocity $v$ of a merry-go-round decreases at a rate that is proportional to the velocity at that moment. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the velocity at time $t?$" 13194139535790 true] [17592186366406 1113 #uuid "307b1396-bf2f-5c6f-b4f9-47e505860659" 13194139535790 true] [17592186366406 1145 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **velocity** $v$ of a merry-go-round **decreases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **velocity** at the moment.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *velocity* of a merry-go-round \nvaries. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *velocity.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}∝v.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the velocity *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-kv.\n$$" 13194139535790 true] [17592186366407 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366408 13194139535790 true] [17592186366407 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366409 13194139535790 true] [17592186366407 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366410 13194139535790 true] [17592186366407 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366411 13194139535790 true] [17592186366407 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366412 13194139535790 true] [1759218